        "id": 5065
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-17T20:37:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The second solution seems a little squirrelly to me -- while we can add a check to UploadInstance::addCommand to skip any uploads with invalid proxies, what happens to any future uploads that were depending on the skipped one? I suppose practically in this case it doesn\u0027t matter because we should have an instantiated proxy for the text atlas, but that just feels like it\u0027s introducing a potential future bug. Also we\u0027d have to rewrite RecordingPriv::addCommands and TaskGraph::addCommands to not bail on the first failure.\n\nI think the real solution is the first one: put the atlas on the Context and have each Recording playback upload glyphs to it dynamically. \n\nI am curious how often promise images fail -- is this something where we need to significantly rewrite our code to protect against it, or it is a bug on the client side?",
      "parentUuid": "2696f6c0_3eeed5fa",
      "revId": "7382cae4b0f6a009125a87c89d1e0e2a23552f09",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
